course: dictionary
lesson: 15249
title: What makes things shiny
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Shininess is the quality of being shiny. A shiny thing looks bright and smooth because it reflects light well. «The shininess of the new spoon made it look almost like a mirror.»
explain: Scientists test shininess to sort materials. Metals are usually shiny, while wood and cloth are usually dull. «Ella tested the shininess of a copper coin and a wooden block.» The shinier one reflected more light.
explain: Shininess is an uncountable noun, so we do not say "two shininesses". We say «the shininess of the lake» or «the shininess of her hair». Use it to describe how much something gleams.
fact: Shininess means how bright, smooth and gleaming a surface looks when light falls on it.
fact: In science, shininess tells us how much a material reflects light.
fact: Metals are usually shiny, so shininess helps us sort metals from other materials.
fact: Smooth surfaces reflect more light, so they often look shinier than rough ones.
fact: «The shininess of the car's paint made it sparkle in the sun.»
exercise: «The shininess of the spoon made it look like a mirror.» What does shininess mean here? | How hot something feels | How loud a sound is | How heavy something is | *How bright and smooth a surface looks
exercise: Which material is usually shiny? | Paper | Cloth | Wood | *Metal
exercise: Which surface is most likely to have high shininess? | *A smooth, polished table | A furry toy | A rough brick wall | A crumpled paper bag
test: In science, what does shininess tell us about a material? | *How much it reflects light | How much it weighs | How warm it is | How it smells
test: Which sentence uses shininess correctly? | *The shininess of her hair caught the sunlight. | The shininess ran away quickly. | Two shininesses sat on the shelf. | She shininessed the door yesterday.
exam: Which word is closest in meaning to shininess? | Heat | Silence | Weight | *Gleam
